#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fd17c91-187c-5849-9648-7b31f2b3be96" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "ea06319a-98d8-5b73-a224-a8c03005b5db" :question/math-academy-id "e-12876" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $10x - 4 > 16.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $4$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x-4 & >16 \\\\ 10x-4+4 & >16+4 \\\\ 10x+0 & >20 \\\\ 10x & >20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $10{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x & >20 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & >\\frac{20}{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{10}x}{\\cancel{10}} & >2 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x> 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192540 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cb884d3-1a4f-56aa-8628-b899f4eefacb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities When Flipping is Required"}] :question/id #uuid "1107a2bf-525e-5a08-9f28-dfd8c72718c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12877" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2x + 3  > -1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3 & >-1 \\\\ -2x+3-3 & >-1-3 \\\\ -2x+0 & >-4 \\\\ -2x & >-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-4 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}x}{\\cancel{-2}}\\, & <\\,\\,2 \\\\ x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x<2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6076650-101c-5fbf-bf47-9de8e6888288" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/id #uuid "fa636b0d-3494-56b7-8be2-b634316f60ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-12878" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-11 \\le     -8y + 5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $5$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-11 & \\le -8y+5 \\\\ -11-5 & \\le -8y+5-5 \\\\ -16 & \\le -8y+0 \\\\ -16 & \\le -8y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-8.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-8y \\\\ \\frac{-16}{-8}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-8y}{-8} \\\\ 2\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{\\cancel{-8}y}{\\cancel{-8}} \\\\ 2\\, & \\ge \\,\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny \\le   2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y \\le   2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504661 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6076650-101c-5fbf-bf47-9de8e6888288" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023bbc6a-3c52-5565-bf3a-b9068e2f0a1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504034} {:answer/id #uuid "0cf264f3-eda3-5c7d-b91e-05b943df2dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504058} {:answer/id #uuid "2a356c0a-5c85-5ef6-89f7-71357f55c704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504108} {:answer/id #uuid "51d31921-a1aa-55dd-9c26-0657fbe6c246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504181} {:answer/id #uuid "fd30a97e-f59d-55a7-a079-e8fc6782015c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cf264f3-eda3-5c7d-b91e-05b943df2dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504058} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f90a6ab-67eb-52cc-8691-87196f6365e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a7f55f36-a99e-57a6-94a7-d395d5c39a69" :question/math-academy-id "q-154276" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-1\\le 5x+14.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $14$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le 5x+14 \\\\ -1-14 & \\le 5x+14-14 \\\\ -15 & \\le 5x+0 \\\\ -15 & \\le 5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15 & \\le 5x \\\\ -\\frac{15}{5} & \\le \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ -3 & \\le \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nx\\ge -3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6076650-101c-5fbf-bf47-9de8e6888288" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality and Adjusting the Final Result"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a716ea-d36d-59e6-9968-a209810ec8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504117} {:answer/id #uuid "5a727ed3-d24a-5b37-b33f-e939b6e82eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504189} {:answer/id #uuid "608213db-29a5-5235-b954-f49ade8d7a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504199} {:answer/id #uuid "9053a33b-2db2-5fb1-8c4e-f480c8a9b8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504287} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1d073-bc8f-514a-9289-687ec7b9889f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9053a33b-2db2-5fb1-8c4e-f480c8a9b8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504287} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d18f9d5-e80e-5bc4-9743-f4a7127d1000" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6bd147ae-a22b-5420-b57b-dd219e2ccfea" :question/math-academy-id "q-154336" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $45>-6y+15.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $15$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}45 & >-6y+15 \\\\ 45-15 & >-6y+15-15 \\\\ 30 & >-6y+0 \\\\ 30 & >-6y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-6.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30\\,\\, & >\\,\\,-6y \\\\ \\frac{30}{-6}\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{-6y}{-6} \\\\ -5\\, & <\\,\\,\\frac{\\cancel{-6}y}{\\cancel{-6}} \\\\ -5\\, & <\\,\\,y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny>-5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504662 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cb884d3-1a4f-56aa-8628-b899f4eefacb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities When Flipping is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4595cb23-916f-51fc-a8c6-3762051425b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4595cb23-916f-51fc-a8c6-3762051425b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504157} :answer-field/id #uuid "c241ff02-e299-5dd2-a055-a3b0bc886249" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b63ce0d-2252-5f73-ad45-e667006e7c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b63ce0d-2252-5f73-ad45-e667006e7c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504246} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4f94d84-354f-5533-9c95-be77f32aca21" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a80bc2bf-80f4-5f0b-bce9-f8d616688e2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-177679" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-5y+16\\le -4$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $16$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y+16 & \\le -4 \\\\ -5y+16-16 & \\le -4-16 \\\\ -5y+0 & \\le -20 \\\\ -5y & \\le -20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-5.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-20 \\\\ \\frac{-5y}{-5}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-20}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}y}{\\cancel{-5}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,4 \\\\ y\\,\\, & \\ge \\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y\\ge 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cb884d3-1a4f-56aa-8628-b899f4eefacb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities When Flipping is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d847024f-d453-512d-88af-bc347ca62fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d847024f-d453-512d-88af-bc347ca62fad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504410} :answer-field/id #uuid "659a3cf2-555b-5d99-8f3e-501ecab03101" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f537108-5876-58bc-8818-e7077c20c274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f537108-5876-58bc-8818-e7077c20c274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504087} :answer-field/id #uuid "a485e9b9-1f0c-5b82-a657-2123599d4351" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0822285c-ebb1-578e-9679-e7a486cbcc58" :question/math-academy-id "q-177680" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-7t+2\\le -5$ is $t${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7t+2 & \\le -5 \\\\ -7t+2-2 & \\le -5-2 \\\\ -7t+0 & \\le -7 \\\\ -7t & \\le -7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-7.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7t\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-7 \\\\ \\frac{-7t}{-7}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-7}{-7} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-7}t}{\\cancel{-7}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,1 \\\\ t\\,\\, & \\ge \\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t\\ge 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fd17c91-187c-5849-9648-7b31f2b3be96" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85367f06-3710-588f-81e1-e0b3b70fd831" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504262} {:answer/id #uuid "8c76e6df-5c8b-5078-8bd1-203abea58a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504279} {:answer/id #uuid "aec9d768-f404-5791-b0e8-e917f7d7cc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504334} {:answer/id #uuid "b63dfdd3-f354-5694-a6c1-24f2d8216435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x<6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504347} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb5730c-6068-553a-a34a-cde9d3e92545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec9d768-f404-5791-b0e8-e917f7d7cc73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504334} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f1d1ff8-ac3c-5aeb-a4f9-20167449027f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0b7f966-d726-5db3-885d-bd379b62b2e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-29069" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2x+2>-10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2 & >-10 \\\\ 2x+2-2 & >-10-2 \\\\ 2x+0 & >-12 \\\\ 2x & >-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & >-12 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & >-\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}x}{\\cancel{2}} & >-6 \\\\ x & >-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504668 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fd17c91-187c-5849-9648-7b31f2b3be96" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0967d231-71f1-546d-8455-04b3a8ea5430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504049} {:answer/id #uuid "0983dc79-ff84-53a4-9f90-117faf58ea22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504051} {:answer/id #uuid "68e9bc65-51e2-5ec3-8741-8952ed767af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504215} {:answer/id #uuid "78c02d26-4f8a-56cb-9548-6779dacc80cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504239} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd44dd3-a9d6-5699-a2d4-b45594249d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e9bc65-51e2-5ec3-8741-8952ed767af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504215} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad88ce2c-c0b4-5896-8791-c75ff580324c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0992f95-7b13-5c5a-ba7a-568131e59eaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-6275" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4x+2\\le 10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & \\le 10 \\\\ 4x+2-2 & \\le 10-2 \\\\ 4x+0 & \\le 8 \\\\ 4x & \\le 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & \\le 2 \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 2.$"}]}
